From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:40:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Yandex: chunked body download (opt-in), skip folders
 without new mail

- BICHON_IMAP_FETCH_CHUNK_KB (crates/core/src/imap/chunked.rs): fetch each
  message on its own in parts of BODY.PEEK[]<offset.N>, as Thunderbird does,
  instead of whole bodies of a batch in one FETCH. Yandex stalls on large
  multi-message responses and drops the connection. A missing part is an
  error: a truncated message is never stored.
- Skip the incremental sync of a folder whose UIDNEXT (from this round's
  STATUS) has not moved past the archived watermark
  (archive/imap/download/unchanged.rs): a round without new mail needs no
  connection per folder.
- Wiring: one hook in uid_batch_retrieve_emails, extract_raw_and_store_it
  next to extract_envelope_and_store_it, classify_imap_error pub(crate).
- Checks cover the new files; tests live in *_tests.rs files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
